# 9. Why This Works

Sorting guarantees:

* Every previous interval starts before (or at the same point as) the current interval.
* If a previous interval also has an end greater than or equal to the current end, then it completely covers the current interval.

Therefore, checking only the largest end (`max_end`) seen so far is enough.

